## Orchestration behavior audit (LocalOrchestrator.cs)

- Implements IWorldOrchestration (the T1 seam from Task 1).
- Constructor takes IRegistry + ILoggerFactory. Resolves WorldService = FantaSim.App.World.IService
  and EcsService = FantaSim.App.Ecs.IService via _registry.TryGet<T>() — real ServiceArchi
  contract interfaces, not trivially-stubbed helpers.
- TriggerAsync dispatches on WellKnownCommands.Generate / Tick / Refresh; unknown commands
  return typed CommandError("unknown-command", ...) without throwing.
- Generate path: parses payload -> builds WorldGenerationRequest -> world.RunGenerationAsync
  -> on success fans out ecs.UpdateAll(0f) (comment explains iii triggers worlds/recipes,
  not per-tick sim). Result serialized as JSON. Missing App.World returns typed
  "missing-service" error naming "FantaSim.App.World.IService".
- Tick path: forwards delta to ecs.UpdateAll(delta). Missing App.Ecs returns typed
  missing-service error.
- Refresh path: world.GetOverviewAsync(), no ECS touch.
- HealthAsync: Ok=true only when both WorldService and EcsService registered; Commands=3.
- No Process.Start, no external clocks, single-threaded deterministic. PASS.

## Iii bridge stub audit (IiiBridgeOrchestrator.cs)

- Implements IWorldOrchestration.
- TriggerAsync and HealthAsync both throw NotImplementedException with documented message:
  "The native iii bridge (Rust/Hermes) is not built in this slice. Use LocalOrchestrator
  for in-process orchestration; this stub exists only to make the IWorldOrchestration seam
  explicit and deferred."
- No process spawning, no App.Agent/App.Stage references. Clearly defers native bridge work.
  PASS.

